## Cause
`FixedOffsetZone` (src/zones/fixedOffsetZone.js) hard-coded `get isValid() { return true; }`, so any value passed to the constructor — including a non-numeric string like `"CDT"` — was reported as a valid zone. `DateTime`'s constructor (`src/datetime.js:385`) and the factories (`fromObject` :531, `fromJSDate` :531, `setZone` :1266) only emit `unsupportedZone(zone)` (`new Invalid("unsupported zone", ...)`, datetime.js:48-50) when `!zone.isValid`, so with `isValid === true` the bogus zone slipped through and the DateTime ended up invalid with reason `"invalid input"` (offset/ts math produced NaN) instead of `"unsupported zone"`.

## Fix (only file changed: /luxon/src/zones/fixedOffsetZone.js)
```diff
-import { formatOffset, signedOffset } from "../impl/util.js";
+import { formatOffset, signedOffset, isNumber } from "../impl/util.js";
@@
   /** @override **/
   get isValid() {
-    return true;
+    return isNumber(this.fixed);
   }
```
This matches the contract used by the other zones (IANAZone caches `isValidZone`, InvalidZone returns `false`) and the docs (docs/zones.md: fixed offsets are numeric offsets like `UTC+7`; named offsets such as EST/CDT are "only supported ... in formatting"). No other behavior changed: `offset()`, `name`, `formatOffset`, `equals`, `universal`, `utcInstance`, `instance()`, `parseSpecifier()` are untouched, and every internal construction site (`normalizeZone`, regexParser, tokenParser) passes numbers.

## Verification
Manual script /tmp/check.js (node + @babel/register, outside repo test dir), "before" = same script run against a pristine copy of src with the bug re-introduced (/tmp/src-before). Diff of outputs:

| case | before | after |
|---|---|---|
| `new FixedOffsetZone("CDT").isValid` | `true` | **`false`** |
| `DateTime.fromMillis(0,{zone}).isValid` | `false` | `false` |
| `DateTime.fromMillis(0,{zone}).invalidReason` | `"invalid input"` | **`"unsupported zone"`** |
| `DateTime.fromMillis(0,{zone}).invalidExplanation` | `u

